diff --git a/packages/ui/src/components/chat/message/parts/DOCUMENTATION.md b/packages/ui/src/components/chat/message/parts/DOCUMENTATION.md
index ba30df1..10cbcb8 100644
--- a/packages/ui/src/components/chat/message/parts/DOCUMENTATION.md
+++ b/packages/ui/src/components/chat/message/parts/DOCUMENTATION.md
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ Use this doc when you ask an agent to change tool/header/description behavior.
 
 ### MCP Apps proof
 
-Web and Electron render `state.metadata.mcp.ui.html` at the start of the expanded
+Web and Electron render `state.metadata.mcp.ui.html` in place of the expanded
 tool result, including empty text and error results. VS Code, hosted mobile and
 Capacitor retain their existing text output. The tool row remains collapsible;
 folding it destroys the app's local state.
@@ -107,10 +107,15 @@ The JSON-RPC adapter supports only `ui/initialize`,
 `ui/notifications/initialized` and `tools/call`. Initialization advertises
 `serverTools: {}` so apps can enable their tool controls. It grants no browser
 permissions, resource access or external origins. Calls after initialization are restricted to the part's MCP
-server, show a visible tool-request status, and use the owning `part.sessionID`
-and session directory. Server-side permission requests still reach PermissionDock.
+server, show a visible tool-request status, and use the owning `part.sessionID`,
+`part.messageID` and session directory. The server checks the message's agent,
+even after the session changes agent. Server-side permission requests still reach PermissionDock.
 Missing ownership fails closed. Exact source-window identity, runtime identity,
 effect cleanup and frame ownership gate requests and asynchronous replies.
+After the initial srcDoc load, any further frame load permanently disables
+requests and replies and aborts pending callbacks. The status shows that the app
+navigated away. Web CSP cannot prevent the outbound navigation itself, a limit
+shared with extension iframes. Electron blocks it in the native navigation hook.
 
 ### Why the extension policy is reused
 
diff --git a/packages/ui/src/components/chat/message/parts/McpAppFrame.tsx b/packages/ui/src/components/chat/message/parts/McpAppFrame.tsx
index 2afdb2d..7049b3e 100644
